  "reproducibility_frictions_observed": [
    "no item-level release exists for any proprietary evaluator (the repository's results/ and the Hugging Face 'predictions' subset cover only the 25 open-source base LLMs), so the comparison is at the accuracy level (one decimal) and the original's sampling error has to be proxied by ours",
    "the repository has no LICENSE (GitHub API license: null): the code may be run but not redistributed; only the Hugging Face data mirror is apache-2.0",
    "ReIFE/base_llm.py imports vllm unconditionally, so even the pure-API arm cannot be imported without a stub, and meta_eval.py needs krippendorff and tabulate, which the repository never declares",
    "the base_pairwise parser resolves an unparsable reply with random.randint(1,2) (a coin flip seeded 42 per output file) instead of recording a miss, so format failures pull accuracy toward 50% rather than showing up; it is also case sensitive ('output (a)' misses) and takes the first 'Output (x)' in the reply, so a 'both are good' answer scores as (a)",
    "the Tier B config's transcription of prompts/pairwise_vanilla.txt is not verbatim (blank lines collapsed, '**equally likely**' unbolded) and its swapped order swaps the output contents where the repository swaps the display positions"
  ]
